    "text": "The segment consists of a 20- to 60-byte header, followed by data from the application program. The header is 20 bytes if there are no options and up to 60 bytes if it contains options. ” Source port address: > 16-bit field defines port number of application program in the sending host. > Destination port address: > 16-bit field defines the port number of application program in receiving host. >» Sequence number: “> 32-bit field defines number assigned to first byte of data contained in this segment. > During connection establishment, each party uses a random number generator to create an initial sequence number (ISN), which is usually different in each direction.",
